# Nothing valuable should be inside this worktree in the first place -- runs,
# generated arms, faucet codes and identity backups live in $GVPN_STATE
# (~/gvpn-state by default), outside the repo, because a push-to-checkout deploy
# rewrites the worktree and `git clean -fdx` empties it.
#
# These entries are a second line of defence for the old layout and for anything
# written here by hand. The FIRST line is tools/scan-secrets.sh, which refuses to
# commit an address even in a file that is supposed to be tracked.

# --- pre-restructure locations, kept so an un-migrated VM stays safe ---------
bench-runs/
faucet-codes
faucet-codes.used
BUILD.txt

# --- state that must never be tracked ---------------------------------------
gvpn-state/
*.safe
*.identity

# arms/ IS tracked: it holds templates, which carry no addresses. Rendered
# instances go to $GVPN_STATE/arms. This catches a rendered one written here by
# mistake -- a template has no config.toml.
arms/*/config.toml
arms/*/arms/*/env
arms/*/.template

# --- noise ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
